infiltrator-software (0.3.71) unstable; urgency=high

  * Route kernel, repository and repair consequences through one explicit app
    coordinator instead of making page views refresh unrelated pages directly.
  * Replace magic navigation-row coupling with named application-page routing.
  * Move System package-engine loading and Repair diagnostics behind dedicated
    data boundaries so GTK views no longer own reconciliation work.
  * Give transaction-review UI and update runtime-state persistence dedicated
    app components and remove those responsibilities from page-view contracts.
  * Narrow the transitional app-shell contract to the few refresh hooks still
    implemented by the legacy shell while preserving existing UI behaviour.

 -- Shannon Smith <infiltratr@yandex.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 20:45:00 +1100

infiltrator-software (0.3.70) unstable; urgency=high

  * Remove pasted console/tool truncation artefacts from the Debian changelog
    and replace the corrupted historical tail with a clean release record;
    older detailed release history remains preserved by immutable Git tags and
    published GitHub releases.
  * Keep VERSION, README, Debian changelog and AppStream release metadata tied
    to one source version through permanent CI source-contract checks.
  * Reject future console/tool truncation markers in authoritative release
    metadata before build or publication.
  * Preserve the 0.3.69 runtime C++ source unchanged while publishing this
    repository-integrity repair through the normal verified release and APT
    pipeline.

 -- Shannon Smith <infiltratr@yandex.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +1100

infiltrator-software (0.3.69) unstable; urgency=high

  * Move public kernel and repository source records into the core model so
    client and UI headers no longer depend on concrete engine/source backends.
  * Move Linux Mint mirror-health probing behind the source boundary and split
    the application state into page-oriented ownership seams.
  * Make Installed native package state strictly engine-owned and replace
    brittle exact-source-layout tests with durable architecture and safety
    contracts.
  * Extract native update reconciliation, Flatpak/Cinnamon update discovery and
    transaction planning from main.cpp into the dedicated Updates controller.
  * Preserve current GTK behaviour while reducing app-shell coupling, with the
    full build, tests, launch smoke, AppStream and Debian package gates retained.

 -- Shannon Smith <infiltratr@yandex.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +1100

