infiltrator-software (0.3.67) unstable; urgency=high

  * Rebuild update rows so Application/System type, Recommended/System-critical
    and Security badges share one title baseline instead of being laid out in
    different vertical coordinate systems.
  * Collapse version and repository metadata into one compact secondary line and
    flatten nested group/item boxes so the update list reads as one hierarchy.
  * Move Select all, Security, Kernel and Clear beside the Available updates
    heading, leaving the top action strip for status, refresh and installation.
  * Tighten Updates-only hero, summary cards, section headers and row geometry
    without changing the current InfiltratorOS colour palette.
  * Add source-contract coverage for the update-row chip alignment and selection
    toolbar placement to prevent the same layout regression returning.

 -- Shannon Smith <infiltratr@yandex.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 18:20:00 +1000
